# AgentOS configuration (copy to .env and adjust)

# API server
PORT=4000
HOST=0.0.0.0
ENVIRONMENT=production
DATABASE_PATH=./apps/api/data/agentos.db

# Session signing secret — CHANGE THIS in any real deployment
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# --- LLM provider -------------------------------------------------------
# The gateway is OpenAI-compatible, so any provider with an OpenAI-style
# /chat/completions endpoint works. If no key is set, the deterministic `mock`
# provider runs every agent (no key needed for the demo).
#
# OpenAI: Provide your OpenAI API key for GPT models (e.g. gpt-4o).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# Hugging Face: paste your HF token (hf_...) as HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY. HF's
# OpenAI-compatible router is used automatically. (You can also set OPENAI_API_KEY
# to an HF token with OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://router.huggingface.co/v1).
HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY=
# HF_TOKEN=                  (alias for HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY)
#
# Gemini / Grok — optional. Provide a GEMINI_API_KEY to enable gemini models (e.g. gemini-1.5-pro).
# Without keys the mock provider still runs every trigger so the outline works with zero setup.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GROK_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
#
# Real Google Sign-In (optional). When unset, the console uses a Google-style
# account picker that creates a workspace from the chosen Gmail.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# NOTE: the legacy `https://api-inference.huggingface.co/v1` host has been
# decommissioned and returns 410/404. Use the router above.
# Seeded agents request `openai:meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct`; on the HF
# router append a provider (e.g. `...:hf-inference` or `...:fastest`) if the
# model is not routable as-is. If the provider call fails the runtime falls
# back to the mock provider, so runs still complete.

# --- Deployment ---------------------------------------------------------
# Railway: SQLite is a local file. Attach a volume and point DATABASE_PATH at
# it (e.g. /data/agentos.db), otherwise the database is wiped on every deploy
# and all accounts, agents, and runs are lost.
# DATABASE_PATH=/data/agentos.db

# The web console proxies /api/* to the API. Resolved at REQUEST time by
# apps/web/app/api/[...path]/route.ts, so changing it and restarting the web
# service is enough — no rebuild required.
# No trailing slash (it is stripped, but other proxies may not be so kind).
# API_URL=https://your-api.up.railway.app
